<h1>Supplemental App Transfer</h1>

<p>
    The Supplemental App Transfer utility extracts data from an old supplemental application and transfers it into a new form. This saves significant time by automatically filling forms with information from previous applications, eliminating manual data entry.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Supplemental App Transfer utility showing: old supplemental application upload area, target form selector, "Update Business Details" checkbox, "Create New Form" button, and the output form preview. Show the before/after comparison. -->

<h2>What the Supplemental App Transfer Does</h2>

<p>
    This utility enables you to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Extract data from old forms</strong> – Uses document intelligence to read information from existing supplemental applications</li>
    <li><strong>Transfer to new forms</strong> – Automatically fills new form templates with extracted data</li>
    <li><strong>Support multiple form types</strong> – Works with various supplemental application formats (Kinsale, Amwins, CS, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>Auto-detect form type</strong> – Can automatically identify which form type to use</li>
    <li><strong>Update business details</strong> – Optionally updates client business information during transfer</li>
    <li><strong>Generate clean output</strong> – Creates a new, properly filled form ready to send or sign</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual diagram showing the transfer workflow: 1) Upload old supplemental app, 2) Select target form, 3) Extract data with AI, 4) Fill new form, 5) Download/output new form. Use icons and progress indicators. -->

<h2>Using the Supplemental App Transfer</h2>

<p>
    To transfer data from an old form to a new one:
</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Upload the old supplemental application</strong> – Drag and drop or select the PDF of the old form you want to extract data from</li>
    <li><strong>Select the target form</strong> – Choose which form template to use:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Autodetect</strong> – Let the system identify the form type automatically</li>
            <li><strong>Kinsale</strong> – Kinsale supplemental application format</li>
            <li><strong>Amwins</strong> – Amwins supplemental application format</li>
            <li><strong>CS</strong> – CS supplemental application format</li>
            <li>Or other available form types</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Configure options</strong>:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Update Business Details</strong> – Check this if you want to update the client's business information in Quickfire with data from the form</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Create the new form</strong> – Click <strong>Create New Form</strong> to start the transfer process</li>
    <li><strong>Monitor progress</strong> – Watch as the system:
        <ul>
            <li>Extracts text from the PDF</li>
            <li>Uses AI to identify and extract form fields</li>
            <li>Fills the new form template</li>
            <li>Attaches the completed form</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Review and use</strong> – Once complete, download or open the output document, then send or sign as usual</li>
</ol>

